site/src/data/thesis-analyst-live-comparisons.ts:4016:                "The 80% interval is justified mainly from two recent annual changes plus qualitative survey/category noise, which is a weak realized-volatility basis.",
site/src/data/thesis-analyst-live-comparisons.ts:4138:          text: "Base 2024 rate 10.8 + expected 2025 net increase 0.5 = 11.3. The 80 percent interval is judgmental rather than a clean long-history volatility estimate: recent annual changes of +0.3 and +0.6, survey/category noise, and policy churn support a +/-0.6 point band, giving 10.7 to 11.9.",
